## Root cause

`ms-postback-relay` is **OOMKilled on boot** (exit 137, 37 restarts). Release `rc-14-2026-10-06-16-05` changed `RetryScheduler.start()` to load **every pending retry into memory** before serving. Yesterday's partner-gateway outage (13:58–15:47 UTC) left **2,184,113 pending rows (~1.4 GB)** in `postback_retries`. Each pod runs out of its 448 MB heap about 40 s into startup.

The release alone was harmless (it shipped at 16:09, after the backlog stopped growing), and so was the backlog alone (the `master` build pages through it 500 rows at a time). Together they keep every replica in a crash loop, so **no postbacks have been delivered since the first restart**.

## Evidence

| Signal | Finding |
|---|---|
| `kubectl describe` | `Last State: Terminated · OOMKilled · 137`, limit `512Mi`, `--max-old-space-size=448` |
| Previous logs | `loading pending retries on boot` → heap 441/448 MB → `JavaScript heap out of memory` |
| Prometheus | Sawtooth from ~90 MiB to 512 MiB in 38–44 s per restart. Flat at 140–170 MiB for 7 days before the rollout |
| Rollout history | Revision 42 → `rc-14-2026-10-06-16-05` at 2026-10-06 16:09 |
| Code @ `rc` | `repo.find({ where: { status: 'pending' } })` with no `take`. `master` uses `take: 500` per tick |
| Postgres | 2.13 M of the pending rows were created 13:00–15:59 on 2026-10-06 |

Tempo has no traces for the service: it never finishes booting, so it never exports a span.

## Fix

Keep boot-time scheduling, but stream it in pages instead of materialising the whole table:

```diff
   async loadPendingRetries(): Promise<void> {
-    const pending = await this.repo.find({ where: { status: 'pending' } });
-    for (const retry of pending) this.queue.push(retry);
+    // Page by id: a backlog after an outage can be millions of rows.
+    let after = 0;
+    for (;;) {
+      const page = await this.repo.find({
+        where: { status: 'pending', id: MoreThan(after) },
+        order: { id: 'ASC' },
+        take: 500,
+      });
+      if (page.length === 0) break;
+      for (const retry of page) this.queue.push(retry.id);
+      after = page[page.length - 1].id;
+    }
   }
```

Queue ids rather than entities. Even paged, 2.2 M full rows would not fit in 448 MB.

## Unblock now (before the fix ships)

1. Roll back to revision 41: `kubectl rollout undo deployment/ms-postback-relay -n native-prod --to-revision=41`. The `master` build drains the backlog 500 rows per tick.
2. Or keep `rc-14` and set `RETRY_SCHEDULER_ON_BOOT=false` until the paged loader is merged.

Drill is read-only, so neither has been applied.

